{"theory":"wzw-models","member":{"at":"(E_6)_1"},"chiral_algebra":"(\\widehat{\\mathfrak{e}}_6)_1","Z_tex":"Z = |\\chi_{\\mathbf{1}}|^2 + |\\chi_{\\mathbf{27}}|^2 + |\\chi_{\\bar{\\mathbf{27}}}|^2","character_tex":"Weyl-Kac characters at $z = 0$: $\\chi_\\lambda(q) = \\eta(q)^{-\\dim G}\\sum_{\\beta\\in Q^\\vee}\\prod_{\\alpha>0}\\frac{(\\alpha,\\lambda+\\rho+K\\beta)}{(\\alpha,\\rho)}\\,q^{|\\lambda+\\rho+K\\beta|^2/2K}$, $K = k + h^\\vee$, long roots of length$^2$ 2 (here $\\dim G = 78$, $h^\\vee = 12$, $K = 13$). One block per integrable highest weight, labelled by the $E_6$ irrep; $h_{\\mathbf{1}} = 0$, $h_{\\mathbf{27}} = \\tfrac{2}{3}$, $h_{\\bar{\\mathbf{27}}} = \\tfrac{2}{3}$.","description":"Diagonal modular invariant of the $E_6$ WZW model at level 1, $c = k\\dim G/(k+h^\\vee) = 6$. Characters from the Weyl-Kac formula specialised to $z=0$ (the finite Weyl sum becomes the Weyl dimension factor and the denominator becomes $\\eta^{\\dim G}$ by the Macdonald identity), summed exactly over the coroot lattice. The generator checks the Macdonald identity, the leading terms $\\dim\\lambda\\, q^{h_\\lambda-c/24}$ and that the weight-1 space of the vacuum module has dimension $\\dim G = 78$, and compares with independent formulas: $E_6$ root-lattice theta functions $\\Theta_{\\lambda+Q}/\\eta^6$; with the partner level-1 theory, $\\sum_i \\chi_i\\tilde\\chi_i = \\chi^{(E_8)_1}$ for $SU(3)_1\\times(E_6)_1$.","generator":"scripts/spectra/gen_wzw.py","c":"6","irreducible":true,"cutoff":"10","s_error":5.8e-16,"gap":"1","blocks":[{"label":"\\chi_{\\mathbf{1}}","h":"0","coeffs":[1,78,729,4382,19917,77274,264644,827388,2400597,6556672,17007594,42225138,100884221]},{"label":"\\chi_{\\mathbf{27}}","h":"2/3","coeffs":[27,378,2484,12312,49896,177660,570807,1695762,4718979,12443436,31323780,75764268]},{"label":"\\chi_{\\bar{\\mathbf{27}}}","h":"2/3","coeffs":[27,378,2484,12312,49896,177660,570807,1695762,4718979,12443436,31323780,75764268]}],"n_blocks":3,"primaries":[{"h":"0",